  * entries that mirror /etc/fstab. Existing nodes are kept as they are (no
  * property is overwritten). Registry entries only: no hardware access. One
  * "N395D" line.
+ *
+ * v396: v395 showed backboardd stop after IOMFB selectors 12, 6, 27, 17, 84,
+ * 50 and the registry lookups of AGXAccelerator and the service name
+ * IOCoreSurfaceRoot (N389I), with no swap ever (N392F sb = se = 0). iOS
+ * 16.7.16 IOSurface.framework _iosConnectInitalize (0x1a3983ca0) looks up
+ * IOServiceNameMatching("IOCoreSurfaceRoot") and, while it is missing, sleeps
+ * one second and retries up to 241 times before IOSurfaceCreate fails
+ * ("IOSurface service not present"): CoreAnimation's render server in
+ * backboardd blocks there for longer than the whole 120 s run. A plain
+ * IOService instance named IOCoreSurfaceRoot (no new class: __DATA_CONST holds
+ * the chain table caves) now opens the existing IOMobileFramebufferUserClient
+ * class, which serves the IOSurface user-client ABI of that framework when its
+ * provider is the surface root: selector 13 limits (0x18 bytes, version 1),
+ * 0 create (binary-serialized properties in, 0xa68-byte surface record out),
+ * 4 lookup (map an existing surface into the caller), traps 2/3 lock/unlock
+ * and 4/5 release (getTargetAndTrapForIndex override, same vtable size).
+ * Surface memory is ordinary pageable kernel memory (IOBufferMemoryDescriptor,
+ * kIOMemoryKernelUserShared) mapped into the caller with one zeroed shared
+ * page after it (the record's second pointer: seed / flags page), 64-byte row
+ * and plane alignment, at most 128 MiB per surface and 192 MiB live in total;
+ * mappings are dropped on release and when the client closes. Other
+ * selectors answer success with zeroed outputs, except value / mach-port
+ * reads (10, 26, 34, 35: unsupported). No Metal device: QuartzCore keeps its
+ * software renderer path ("Failed to initialize Metal or OpenGLES contexts!").
+ * No register, MMIO, interrupt or DMA. Trace: N396R publish, N396O open,
+ * N396S first call of each selector and every failure, N396C each create,
+ * N396T first lock / release trap and failures (shared cap 128).
  */
